WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.070 align:start position:0%
 
beautiful bays  crystal clear water and mild  temperatures all year round  the east coast of cyprus is a favorite  destination for seaside vacationers  one of the island's most idyllic beaches  is fig tree bay  a lot of people come from everywhere to  see the area here  they come to victory bay i have their  water sports since  1975 i used to be in the middle of the  beach  i used to have one boat one pedal  one canoe and a few  wind surfing boards that's it now you  see  what we have those who are looking for a  bit of culture head southwest  to the port city of larnica  the main landmark of the old quarter is  the 9th century church of saint lazarus  hotels line the promenade along  finocuda's beach  named for the palm trees planted along  the shore  boat rides leave the harbor for an  underwater tourist attraction  the xenobia is the largest wreck in the  mediterranean that can be reached by  scuba  it sank in 1980 just two kilometers off  larnica  with more than 100 trucks on board  people travel from other countries to  visit zenobia that is full of groupers  barragudas the marine life down there is  amazing  we are talking about the wreck that is  180 meters so we talk about the mountain  of steel under the water  uh it's something unique for tires okay  guys make your way down and get yourself  sorted out please oh i'm quite nervous  because it's so deep  all of the participants have to prove  that they've got a certain number of  scuba diving hours to be allowed to  explore the zenobia even the pros have  to make the dive  with an instructor  the more experienced divers can go all  the way down  to the hold of the zenobia at a depth of  40 meters  novices stay near the shipwreck surface  about 15 meters deep  it was huge it was really really massive  yeah i love that  further inland there's plenty more to  discover  cyprus has the most extensive forests of  any mediterranean island  at the foot of the trodos mountains lie  a number of idyllic villages  one of the oldest is lafu with its  typical stone houses and narrow alleys  here they brew coffee according to  cypriot tradition  in a copper pot on a bed of hot sand  a few kilometers away wineries produce  one of the oldest wines in the world  comanderia it's a sweet wine made  nowhere else but here  for almost 3 000 years when the gravy is  very sweet we harvest the grapes  and we lay under the strong sun in those  days there is really strong  sunlight for eight to ten days  the sun the graves will lose a lot of  moisture  because of evaporation  and after we collect and take to the  winery where we crash and take the juice  immediately  the grapes are sun-dried and that gives  the wine its amber color  its higher alcohol content also means it  keeps for longer periods of time  after a wine tasting it's worth a trip  westward to aphrodite's rock  this is where the goddess of love is  said to have emerged from the sea  one of many legends surrounding the site  we've heard about the legend and you're  supposed to swim  three times uh clockwise three times  uh counterclockwise and you'll be young  forever  um we haven't done we haven't done it  yet  so let's just say tomorrow okay yeah  tomorrow  according to another variant couples who  swim around the rock will be blessed  with eternal love  and even if the eternal love or eternal  youth doesn't work out  you'll still be rewarded with a  spectacular sunset

